# Security

- Never log, print, or include tokens in error messages (`sprites.token`, `modal.token_id`, `modal.token_secret`).
- Example config files must use empty placeholders, not real credentials.
- Do not execute user input via shell (`sh -c`); when exec is implemented, pass argv slices only.
- Prefer env and config file for secrets; avoid long-lived secrets in command-line flags.
- Validate provider names and paths before use; reject traversal in explicit `--config` paths when validating existence.
